      "utils/http.py"
    ],
    "feature": "Cache-Control directive matching is too strict: it does exact token membership, so RFC 9111 \"qualified\" directive forms like `Cache-Control: private=\"Set-Cookie\"` or `no-store=\"x\"` are not recognized as `private` / `no-store`, which can let a response that should never be shared get stored in a shared cache. Fix the directive handling so a directive is recognized by its name regardless of any qualified `=\"...\"` value (strip the qualifier and surrounding whitespace, compare the lowercased name). Apply the same robust matching everywhere a Cache-Control directive name is checked (the response-caching middleware and the conditional GET / ETag path) so they stay consistent, and so malformed input like `no-store=\"x\"` correctly suppresses the ETag instead of being silently ignored."
  },
